Let β > 1 be a Pisot number, that is, a real algebraic integer greater than 1 all of whose Galois conjugates (other than β itself) lie strictly inside the open unit disk in the complex plane. Set
   B = {0, ±1, ±2, …, ±⌊β⌋} ⊂ ℤ,
where ⌊·⌋ denotes the floor function. Let
   ℤ[1/β] = { Σ_{i=−N}^{M} a_i β^{i} : N, M ∈ ℤ_{≥0}, a_i ∈ ℤ }
be the ring generated by 1/β over ℤ, and let
   B[1/β] = { Σ_{i=−N}^{M} b_i β^{i} : N, M ∈ ℤ_{≥0}, b_i ∈ B }
be the set of all such expressions whose digits are restricted to lie in B. Prove or disprove that
   ℤ[1/β] ∩ [0, 1) = B[1/β] ∩ [0, 1);
equivalently, show that every nonnegative element of ℤ[1/β] in the unit interval admits a finite representation Σ_{i ≥ 1} b_i β^{−i} with all digits b_i ∈ B.

